    "type": "question",
    "label": "35",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following, expressing roots as fractional exponents. $x\\sqrt{x}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^{\\frac32}$, $x\\ge0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x\\sqrt{x}&=x\\times x^{\\frac12}\\\\x\\sqrt{x}&=x^{1+\\frac12}\\\\x\\sqrt{x}&=x^{\\frac32}\\end{align*}$$The original square root requires $x\\ge0$ over the reals.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
